},"title":["Vṛndāyai tulasī-devyai"],"verses":[{"text":["vṛndāyai tulasī-devyai","    priyāyai keśavasya cha","kṛṣṇa-bhakti-prade devi","    satyavatyai namo namaḥ"],"translation":["I eternally offer my respects unto Śrī Vṛndādevī, Śrīmatī Tulasī Mahārāṇī, who is the dearmost object of Lord Keśava’s affection. I bow down before Satyavatī who can bestow pure dedication unto Lord Krishna."],"isLong":false},{"text":["atha natvā mantra-gurūn","    gurūn bhāgavatārthadān","vyāsān jagat-gurūn natvā","    tato jayam udīrayet"],"translation":["Then, let me bow down before all my spiritual masters: the guru who gave me the divine mantra, as well as all those who have taught me the meaning of Śrīmad Bhāgavatam. Let me offer my respectful obeisances unto Śrīla Vyāsadeva, the spiritual master of the entire universe and the giver of the all-conquering conclusions of Śrīmad Bhāgavatam."],"isLong":false},{"text":["jayaḥ sa-parikara śrī-śrī-guru-gaurāṅga-gāndharvā-govindasundar-pādapadmānāṁ jayastu!"],"translation":["Let the holy lotus feet of Śrī Gurudeva, Śrīman Mahāprabhu, and Śrī Śrī Gāndharvā-Govindasundar, along with Their eternal associates, be victorious over all!"],"isLong":true}],"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":true,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en-2022/vrindayai-tulasi-devyai/","description":"vṛndāyai tulasī-devyai. Vṛndāyai tulasī-devyai — a Vaiṣṇava song with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Vṛndāyai tulasī-devyai | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-2022","slug":"vrindayai-tulasi-devyai"}}